    "updated_at": "2025-11-06T22:46:54Z",
    "body": "Thanks for spotting this, I am fixing the test here: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7127725\n\nThe test has two checks for the selectedcontent element being updated in a disconnected subtree which seem to have different behavior because the selectedcontent element only gets updated on insertion if it gets connected to the document since it is using the post-insertion steps instead of the insertion steps.\n\nTo elaborate:\n```javascript\nconst select = document.createElement('select');\nselect.innerHTML =\n`<option>one</option>\n<option>two</option>`;\n\nconst selectedcontent = document.createElement('selectedcontent');\nselect.appendChild(selectedcontent);\n// selectedcontent does NOT get updated here because the element is not\n// connected to the document so the post-connection steps do not run.\n\nselect.value = 'two';\n// selectedcontent does get updated here because the select.value setter steps\n// update the selectedcontent regardless of whether it is connected or not.\n```",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
